    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d875">

                <pb facs="0926" n="806" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg806"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Eddy to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-09-15"><hi rendition="#italic">September 15,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 205.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that I
                    received to-day at 4 o’ clock a note from Count Lamsdorff relating to the
                    removal of discriminating customs duties on certain products of American
                    manufacture and officially notifying this embassy that on August 28 (September
                    10) His Majesty the Emperor issued an imperial order abrogating these duties, to
                    take effect at once.</p>
                <p>Immediately on receipt of the said note, of which a copy and translation are
                    herewith inclosed, I cabled you the contents thereof. * * *</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Spencer Eddy.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d875-a1.xml" xpointer="d875-a1"/>
            </div>
